      "en": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "When I proclaim the providence of Hashem, (which I am now going to focus on in Minchah) it will become clear to all that everyone must ascribe greatness to (and therefore praise) Hashem, our God."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 0
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(I am standing here because I do want to daven, create a relationship, and thank You for all the good You do for me—which is sometimes hard to see or understand—and I want to ask You for the help I need. But that does not come easy to me for so many reasons. Therefore, I am asking, please) Hashem, open my lips and help me express myself properly."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 1
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You Hashem, are the Source of everything, You control everything, and have taken care of Bnei Yisrael throughout our history starting from the time of the Avos. You are all-powerful, You shower us with acts of helpful kindness (even though at times it is hard to see that), and everything is Yours. When dealing with us, You take into account the good deeds of our ancestors, and (everything You do for us is in order to) bring Mashiach to us, their descendants, even if we do not deserve it!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 2
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "זָכְרֵנוּ לְחַיִּים—Please, Hashem, remember us for life; מֶלֶךְ חָפֵץ בַּחַיִּים—for You are our King Who desires life; וְכָתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר הַחַיִּים—and write us in the book of life; לְמַעַנְךָ אֱלֹהִים חַיִּים—so that we may be able to continue to serve You and live up to our potential."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "מֶלֶךְ עוֹזֵר וּמוֹשִׁיעַ וּמָגֵן—You are our King, You have the power to help us through our difficulties, to save us (from our physical and spiritual enemies), and to protect us (from evil). בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה—You Hashem, are the Source of everything; מָגֵן אַבְרָהָם—You are the Protector of Avraham (and us, his descendants)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 3
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "אַתָּה גִּבּוֹר לְעוֹלָם—Hashem, Your power and rulership are permanent; You bring about Techiyas Hameisim (since our souls are eternal); and You have unlimited power to save us."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 5
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You make the winds blow and cause the rain to fall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You cause the dew to fall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "מְכַלְכֵּל חַיִּים בְּחֶסֶד—You take care of us with Your kindness; and with Your great mercy You revive the dead (literally, Techiyas Hameisim, and You also save those who are near physical or spiritual death); You support those"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 6
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "who have fallen (physically and spiritually); You heal the sick (both physically and emotionally ill) and free those in prison (whether in real prisons or trapped in their own sense of limitations); and You keep the covenant You made with our ancestors. There is no other power like You at all; You have total control over our lives and our ultimate salvation. (And that is why we are turning to You and only You with the upcoming requests in our Shemoneh Esrei.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "There is no one like You, our merciful Father;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 7
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Who remembers us, His creations, for life;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "with mercy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "We have total faith that You will perform Techiyas Hameisim."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 8
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You, Hashem, are the Source of everything;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 2
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Who performs Techiyas Hameisim. (Even though it has not yet happened, we are so sure that it will happen that we say this brachah in the present tense!)"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 9
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Let us declare the kedushah of \"שמך\"—all that Hashem does in this world;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 10
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "just like the angels declare the kedushah of \"אותו\"—the essence of Hashem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "As the Navi tells us;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "that one angel calls to the other (so that they all praise Hashem in unison) and say:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The sanctity of Hashem can be felt in all worlds, from the very highest world of angels down to the very lowest world, our material world;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 11
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "His Presence can be felt everywhere (though it requires effort and diligence in order to tap into it through Torah and mitzvos)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Correspondingly, other angels offer praise and declare (as we do now also):"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 13
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The essence of Hashem is completely beyond us (even the highest angels); it is מִמְּקוֹמוֹ—from His place (up there, it all makes sense!)."
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 15
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In addition, it is written in Your holy words:"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 17
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The Kingship of Hashem is for all eternity (He will always be there for us, unlike our mortal helpers); אֱלֹהַיִךְ צִיּוֹן—and Hashem has a special providence on Eretz Yisrael; לְדֹר וָדֹר—in all generations: our past and our future; הַלְלוּיָהּ—whatever happens, praise Hashem!"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 19
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "We will proclaim Your greatness and Your holiness from generation to generation, forever, because You are truly a great and Kadosh King. בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה יְהֹוָה—You, Hashem, are the Source of everything; הָאֵל הַקָּדוֹשׁ—the Almighty, the Kadosh One. (During Aseres Yemei Teshuvah say instead: הַמֶּלֶךְ הַקָּדוֹשׁ—the King, the Kadosh One.) (If you forgot—see Appendix 12:1)"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 21
        }
      ],
