              "text": "FAQ: Why should I bother making requests from Hashem? I've asked Him many times before for stuff, and He keeps on saying no!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "ANSWER: Both very crucial questions for a serious Ben Torah and Bas Yisrael! See Appendix 1."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "During Aseres Yemei Teshuvah add: (If you forgot—see Appendix 12:1) זָכְרֵנוּ לְחַיִּים, מֶלֶךְ חָפֵץ בַּחַיִּים, וְכָתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר הַחַיִּים, לְמַעַנְךָ אֱלֹהִים חַיִּים:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "instant_insight",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Instant Insight: The terms מוֹשִׁיעַ, עוֹזֵר, and מָגֵן represent three levels of help that we need in our lives—from the least to the most. עוֹזֵר—\"help,\" is when we are on the right track, doing what we need to do in the best way possible, and we ask Hashem to please help us that all should work out, since nothing will come to fruition without His help. מוֹשִׁיעַ—\"salvation,\" is when we are completely at a loss; we throw up our hands and say to Hashem, \"Save me, I have no idea what to do next!\" The third and highest level, מָגֵן—\"protect,\" is when we think we're on the right track and think we know what we're doing, but in truth we are completely off base! We ask Hashem, \"If I'm going in the wrong direction—מָגֵן—protect me from myself!\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
